  "description": "XIPRIA crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C128 H120 Gd4 N12 O22,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.628-3.891 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.39-112.02°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C132H124Gd4N14O22. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
